BanMido wrote:
>
> I am playing as a lawful Samurai and I found a chaotic altar at level
> 1. I used it for beatitude testing for sometime but as I progressed,
> it got quite tedious to go all the way back to level 1 to use the
> altar. The gnomish mines entrance was at level 2, hence the level 1
> chaotic altar was the closest one. I was unable to convert the altar
> during my beatitude testing visits, as no monsters were generated on
> that level after my initial run through that level. At that time, I
> did not have any means to create monsters for sacrificing either.

Once you have acceptable armor the number of items that have to be
shuttled for BUC checks does go down significantly.  Especially if you
have a bag of holding the price of shuttling items other than armor,
weapons, stones and containers is not much higher than moving around the
dungeon.  I go up and down a lot with valkyries during the quest just to
be able to eat all of those giants to max out my strength so the price
is not that out of line for a samurai.  It's an over preparation
strategy but it works.

> So, is there any chance that my Samurai will see an altar, from here
> onwards? I believe that an aligned altar will never be generated in
> Gehennom. I haven't reached Medusa yet so not sure how many "aligned
> altar eligible" levels are left before I enter Gehennom.

I would explore to the Castle as it is now only a few more levels.

> And out of curiosity, what does one usually do if he/she cannot find a
> co-aligned altar in a game, assuming that Minetown was a bones level
> where the altar was destroyed? I understand that the odds of such a
> thing happening are vanishingly small but still, out of curiosity...

I like to have an unconverted altar just in case I am desparate for
unholy water but if there are none in the main dungeon until several
levels below Sokoban I'll go back and kill the mine town priest to have
an altar to convert.  The price is high but it's straight forward for a
strong character with a pick axe and a ton of missiles.


